  "_comment": "The methods the hardened engine never binds: the one copy. Every ClassName::method below is never registered in ClassDB on a hardened template (patches/harden.patch, the bind-path hook), so no script, Callable, Object.call or ClassDB lookup can reach it. scripts/deny-header.py generates the C++ header the hook includes from this file at build time; check/check.gd proves a built engine has none of them. Whole classes go in the build profile's disabled_classes instead (profile/trim.gdbuild). Adding or dropping a method is an edit here, not to the patch.",
